index 2045e55..3fb8fcc 100644
--- a/docs/Reference/Routes.md
+++ b/docs/Reference/Routes.md
@@ -120,6 +120,21 @@ fastify.route(options)
   [`handlerTimeout`](./Server.md#factory-handler-timeout). Must be a positive
   integer. When the timeout fires, `request.signal` is aborted and a 503 error
   is sent through the error handler (which can be customized per-route).
+* `concurrency`: limits the number of requests executing this route. It accepts:
+  * `max` (required): positive integer number of admitted requests.
+  * `queueLimit` (optional): non-negative integer number of waiting requests;
+    defaults to `0`. A request arriving when this queue is full receives a 503
+    `FST_ERR_ROUTE_CONCURRENCY_QUEUE_FULL` error.
+  * `queueTimeout` (optional): positive integer maximum wait in milliseconds;
+    defaults to `30000`. An expired queued request receives a 503
+    `FST_ERR_ROUTE_CONCURRENCY_QUEUE_TIMEOUT` error.
+
+  Admission is FIFO and happens before `onRequest` hooks and body parsing.
+  Queue waiting is not included in `handlerTimeout`. Slots remain occupied for
+  the complete response lifecycle and are released on completion, errors,
+  streaming or hijacked-response completion, handler timeout, and client
+  disconnect. Each configured route has independent admission state; routes
+  without this option keep the normal request path.
 * `logLevel`: set log level for this route. See below.
 * `logSerializers`: set serializers to log for this route.
 * `config`: object used to store custom configuration.
